# Line endings matter for the Mac launcher.
#
# "Start Race Manager.command" is a bash script run by macOS. With CRLF
# endings the shebang reads as "/bin/bash\r" and macOS refuses it with
#   bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M
# on the very first double-click. It is authored and packaged on Windows,
# so force LF for shell scripts regardless of the local git config.
*.command text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf

# .bat files are read by cmd.exe and must keep CRLF.
*.bat     text eol=crlf

# Deliberately no "* text=auto": that would renormalise every existing
# file in the repo in one noisy commit.
